    "raw": "Given:\n- 20 gyms\n- Each gym has 10 bikes, 5 treadmills, and 5 elliptical machines\n- Bikes cost $700 each\n- Treadmills cost 50% more than bikes\n- Elliptical machines cost twice as much as treadmills\n\nFirst, calculate the cost of each type of machine:\n- Bikes: $700 each\n- Treadmills: 50% more than bikes = $700 * 1.5 = $1050 each\n- Elliptical machines: Twice the cost of treadmills = $1050 * 2 = $2100 each\n\nNext, calculate the total cost for each type of machine per gym:\n- Bikes per gym: 10 bikes * $700 = $7000\n- Treadmills per gym: 5 treadmills * $1050 = $5250\n- Elliptical machines per gym: 5 elliptical machines * $2100 = $10500\n\nNow, calculate the total cost for all 20 gyms:\n- Total cost for bikes: 20 gyms * $7000 = $140000\n- Total cost for treadmills: 20 gyms * $5250 = $105000\n- Total cost for elliptical machines: 20 gyms * $10500 = $210000\n\nFinally, add up the total costs for all machines:\n- Total cost = $140000 (bikes) + $105000 (treadmills) + $210000 (elliptical machines) = $455000\n\nFINAL: 455000",
